	(text "DIRECT IGNITER DRIVE\nQ2 switches the igniter low-side from the 7 V bench supply.\nNo relay, and no galvanic isolation: J5.2 ties the supply return\nstraight to GNDPWR, so the ~7 A firing pulse returns through the\nboard ground.  Keep the supply leads short and away from the\nload-cell wiring, and route GNDPWR as its own trace.\nIgniter fires ONLY when Q2 is on AND SW2 is closed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 281.686 199.136 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0dcdf960-b30d-400d-aa2d-381e0fd8160f")
	)
	(text "HX711 VCC and R1/R7 pull-ups run at 3.3V:\nTeensy 4.1 pins are NOT 5V tolerant."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.192 87.884 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "33e8d2aa-0956-4867-a756-428d41c387ce")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTES\n\n1 Don't forget buttons need software debounce too.\n\nSTILL TO DO\n-  UHX711 - needs a custom footprint. Left blank. Modeled on Sparkfun.\n-  SW1/SW2/SW3 footprints depend on the buttons and toggle are available\n-  Q1 drives the solenoid coil (~2.4 A peak); Q2 drives the igniter\n   directly at ~7 A - the relay is gone, so Q2 must stay beefy.\n##  Firing current: Estes igniter is ~1 R, so 7 V gives ~7 A.\n   Q2 = IRLB8721PBF, 62 A / 30 V, 8.7 mR at Vgs 4.5 V.  Gate drive\n   here is 3.3 V, so Rds(on) is worse than the datasheet figure -\n   fine for a sub-second pulse; do not lengthen it."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 20.32 233.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58098d34-a08a-411a-95fc-55f5ef50324a")
	)
	(text "BURPG HIP  -  Rev DD  (single-prop liquid motor test stand)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66af09d6-a045-48c6-82c3-5e81fcf91d8c")
	)
	(text "Dedicated Hardware Toggle Switch with Fuse to seperate\nthe igniter from its dedicated power supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.434 170.434 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7b1f1c88-6869-4212-84d9-5da1853db18c")
	)
	(text "12v in from screw terminals:\nLeads into our grounding segregation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.928 38.862 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "94c4f782-434f-4f52-9f4f-b2e88ea7f4ff")
	)
	(text "Screw Terminals for igniter\nand power supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 347.726 167.894 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a4b35326-036d-4b63-bd82-59468caf374a")
	)
	(text "SOLENOID CHANNEL\n0.1 mH / 5 R  ->  I = 12 / 5 = 2.4 A: Load\ntau = L/R = 20 us: Switching time\nI(t) = 2.4 × (1 − e^(−t/tau))\nt = 5, current = 100 %\nRds(on) = 22mOhms from data sheet\nP(Q1) = I^2 x Rds(on) = 2.4^2 x 0.022 = 0.127 W: power in on state\nE = 0.5 x L x I^2 = 0.29 mJ \nD1 Vforward = about .7 v (property of silicon)\nDrain will stay at about 12.7 before Diode provides a path to back to supply\n(steady state clamp approximation)\nAt power off, D1 will experience all 2.4A and disipate that\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 216.154 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aeca85ca-0464-4b0e-9bc4-0c866e344ec1")
	)
	(text "Igniter switched low-side by Q2 (IRLB8721PBF)\nfrom a 7 V bench supply - no relay"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.802 112.014 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "dd429b9c-93e6-45c5-8690-734a86e3674e")
	)
	(text "Solenoid Driver circuit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.354 138.176 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e0722e8c-8337-41e2-84b0-42222c601de1")
	)
	(text "Buck Converter:\nprotect AC ground signals from\nswitching noise on the power rails\nProvides clean and safe 5v power for Teensy\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 117.856 42.672 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
